          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:757316423a5b1f95b14b1ebaac56e612af026bb50f06c1748e688e65a8a17b67"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5f122fec3f8f4850be2bc516d24b08c6",
      "statement": "init_chat_model function has three overload signatures: one returning a fixed BaseChatModel when model is specified with no configurable_fields, one returning a _ConfigurableModel when model is None and no configurable_fields, and one returning _ConfigurableModel when any configurable_fields specification is provided.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/chat_models/base.py#L196-L226",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:735767f0ee6cc07f2f21d7dff4cc4ca193dbd136884971f5a6f8b2ee947e0ec5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a053643fbeda4652babd3eeef4c67584",
      "statement": "The _parse_model function extracts provider prefixes from model identifiers using colon separation, falls back to provider inference via _attempt_infer_model_provider, normalizes provider names to lowercase with underscores, and raises ValueError with suggestions if provider cannot be determined.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/chat_models/base.py#L623-L651",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0f3986f6ea39cbaccfb49ef380d145f3efc5306c2d8faba7cb4e99ecd6236f53:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b9c8a5294dba402d9590f5669a61b448",
      "statement": "Provider inference from model names uses case-insensitive prefix matching for 11 provider patterns (openai: gpt-, o1, o3, chatgpt, text-davinci; anthropic: claude; bedrock: amazon., anthropic., meta.; mistral: mistral, mixtral; and others). Gemini prefix currently defaults to google_vertexai but is deprecated in favor of google_genai.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/chat_models/base.py#L547-L620",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a9fa9d961e85cbbccd7d57b4421babf5fbe5d93a7aa62b3bc0b38d6b368121dc:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_38557dafafff461f8718d5371c3548ad",
      "statement": "The _BUILTIN_PROVIDERS dictionary contains 30 entries mapping provider names to module paths, class names, and creator functions. Each provider entry enables dynamic module import and instantiation. Most providers use the standard _call creator; HuggingFace uses from_model_id, IBM uses model_id mapping, and LangSmith wraps instantiation with gateway configuration.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/chat_models/base.py#L56-L99",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a0432456fbcc294961073b737c0871eb2e1444b6649f4f39c8fd5af7d29f8834:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_342f2c78b5dc45eba70ae2f0459f8ee8",
      "statement": "The _ConfigurableModel wrapper implements lazy instantiation: it defers actual chat model creation until invoke/stream/batch time, extracts configurable parameters from config[\"configurable\"] dict using config_prefix namespacing, merges them with defaults, and instantiates the underlying model. Declarative operations (bind_tools, with_structured_output) are queued and applied after model instantiation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/chat_models/base.py#L661-L731",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d646d99f2edf5883ed0c4b0fb49d519c1cb7662c5c084c9caaa79c6ca74584a8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_018b1b57dfc946d0ba9cddf7f81386f5",
      "statement": "The configurable_fields parameter controls runtime configurability: None creates a fixed model, \"any\" makes all parameters configurable, list/tuple specifies individual parameter names. When model is None and configurable_fields is not specified, configurable_fields defaults to (\"model\", \"model_provider\"). Security warning applies when configurable_fields=\"any\" allows api_key and base_url override.",
      "evidence": [
